§ dependency-tree delta ← phase-A progress                             ⊞
═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

  before Session-13 :
    Rust : 50+ transitive crates (tokio + tower-lsp + serde + regex + ...)
    Python : cryptography , hashlib (optional), jsonschema ...
    OS : sha256sum (optional)

  replaced-or-eliminated Session-13 :
    ✗ levenshtein crate       → Odin parser/levenshtein.odin + --distance
    ✗ Python cryptography     → Odin core:crypto/ed25519 via --sign/--verify
    ✗ hashlib (m2_audit side) → Odin parser/sha256.odin + --sha256
    ✗ os sha256sum            → parser.exe --sha256 (drop-in)

  remaining (Session-14+ targets) :
    D10 serde_json              → A4 Odin JSON parser+emitter (~1000 LOC)
    D11 blake3                  → A2 BLAKE3 Odin (~800 LOC)
    D13 regex + regex-automata  → A8 Regex engine (~2000 LOC)
    D17 url                     → A7 URI parser (~400 LOC)
    D40 cryptography (Python)   → stub ; use parser.exe path
    D41 sentence-transformers   → OPTIONAL (not in critical path)
    D45 latexmk                 → install texlive (P2.1 Session-14)

  net Rust-crate reduction : 1 direct dep removed (levenshtein) +
    transitives not-yet. Bigger reduction arrives with tokio-rewrite
    in phase-B (Session-15+).

═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
§ Apocky-blanket-authority decisions made                              D>
═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

  D1 : Ed25519 via Odin stdlib (not scratch-port)
       ← rationale in DECISIONS.md 2026-04-17 entry ;
         shipping working crypto now > 800-LOC curve math duplicate
  D2 : audit-chain schema evolution via optional-fields not-migration
       ← v1 entries byte-identical ; v2 entries append binary_hash ;
         future v3+ can extend the same pattern
  D3 : cli-daemon = mmap-retention (not interactive-mode)
       ← llama-perplexity.exe b8827 lacks --interactive ; pre-authorized
         fallback ; achieves the 3× target via OS page-cache reuse
  D4 : ctx raise 64 → 256 + 1.8× safety factor
       ← ctx=256 is the new default ; safety factor required to survive
         glyph-heavy tokenization ; C2 anomaly documented as trade
  D5 : LaTeX goldens regen with emit_latex.odin fix
       ← the prior goldens captured a defect ; regen is a bug-fix, not
         a breaking schema change ; documented in commit message

